00:02:14.200 --> 00:02:16.160
that I am a hope dealer.

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:18.720
And like, nobody is going to pick me and you up, Evan.

00:02:18.720 --> 00:02:20.360
Nobody's going to say, get up.

00:02:20.360 --> 00:02:21.240
Come on.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.800
Let me just bottle feed you.

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:23.320
Come on.

00:02:23.320 --> 00:02:24.200
Yeah, it's OK.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.800
Nobody's going to do that.

00:02:25.800 --> 00:02:30.280
And if we don't learn how to focus on the big picture,

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:32.600
focus on I might be down today, but I'm

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:34.040
getting my butt back up.

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:34.960
I ain't staying here.

00:02:34.960 --> 00:02:38.280
I might have a meltdown, but I'm not staying here.

00:02:38.280 --> 00:02:39.840
And so I think that's what it is.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:43.400
That's where I found out that, man, I live to give hope.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:47.340
And it's so much easier, Evan, to be happy.

00:02:47.340 --> 00:02:48.720
Happiness is a choice.

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:50.560
Even when things aren't going right,

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:53.920
even when we're in a pandemic and you're getting furloughed

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:57.680
and you're losing your job and you're fearful,

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:59.120
you know what I'm saying?

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:01.840
Nothing is going to change that.

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:04.600
We're here, except the way you think of things.

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:07.040
And you realize that as long as I got a pulse,

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:08.360
God's got a plan.

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.760
And so that's where Hope Dealer came in.

00:03:10.760 --> 00:03:12.160
I just bounced, man.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:13.240
I bounced back up.

00:03:13.240 --> 00:03:15.280
I fall and I get back up again.

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:18.880
And talk to us about developing your voice,

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:21.000
because you found your voice.

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:23.800
It's, you're unabashedly you.

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.480
And we've had other pastors on

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:29.920
and they don't have the same energy or buoyancy

00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.640
or just loudness, right?

00:03:31.640 --> 00:03:35.400
And it's refreshing and it's different and it's awesome.

00:03:35.400 --> 00:03:37.920
And I don't know if this was always you

00:03:37.920 --> 00:03:40.320
or you kind of came through this journey.

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.680
So tell us about how you found your voice

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:45.200
and you're so willing and courageous

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.800
to step into it every day.

00:03:46.800 --> 00:03:49.920
Well, you know what, I was raised in a religion

00:03:49.920 --> 00:03:53.520
that basically said women couldn't preach.

00:03:53.520 --> 00:03:57.880
Women were only good for having babies, cooking supper.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:04:01.280
And here I am in this very strict religion

00:04:01.280 --> 00:04:04.080
that everybody in this religion looked miserable.

00:04:04.080 --> 00:04:05.120
Everybody in this religion,

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:07.240
like the whole time my daddy was a preacher

00:04:07.240 --> 00:04:08.760
and I'd be looking up at them

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:10.440
and they'd be singing about Jesus

00:04:10.440 --> 00:04:12.600
and they all look like they're about to cut their wrist.

00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:14.960
And I remember at about seven years old,

00:04:14.960 --> 00:04:15.920
looking up there and thinking,

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:17.520
if I've got to go to heaven with y'all

00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:21.320
and spend eternity with y'all, I'd rather go to hell.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:22.560
You know what I'm saying?

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:25.800
This is gonna be the most boring party in heaven ever.

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.960
And so I did this, I was on this perpetual cycle.

00:04:29.960 --> 00:04:33.320
I was in religion, I stayed in it,

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.640
but I kept having my mind because I'm that rebel.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:37.360
I'm kind of a rebel for Jesus.

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:39.960
And I found myself at 36.

00:04:39.960 --> 00:04:41.880
36 was the golden number for me

00:04:41.880 --> 00:04:44.760
because I had to move back in with my mom and dad

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:47.960
at 36 after a 17 year marriage ended.

00:04:47.960 --> 00:04:50.880
And I had never heard from God for myself.

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:55.000
I had all my life put myself in this box

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.360
and I was trying to be an Ann Taylor

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.160
when God created me to be a Betsy Johnson.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.200
I was like, this is boring.

00:05:03.200 --> 00:05:06.520
So coming out of this 17 year marriage,

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:12.560
I really started finding myself and I found God for me.

00:05:12.800 --> 00:05:14.520
I found out, I didn't want the God

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:15.760
that my mom and dad taught me about.

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:19.200
I wanted the God that I knew created the heaven

00:05:19.200 --> 00:05:22.200
and the earth and didn't write me off.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.840
He didn't take me off the clearance rack

00:05:24.840 --> 00:05:26.320
and put me on the clearance rack

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:27.880
because I made some mistakes.

00:05:27.880 --> 00:05:31.840
He knew before I was ever even thought in my mother's womb.

00:05:31.840 --> 00:05:34.640
Evan, he knew that I was gonna be stubborn.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:37.200
He knew that I was gonna walk through this divorce

00:05:37.200 --> 00:05:39.360
and be the only one in my family that can't keep a man.

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:40.600
You know what I'm saying?

00:05:40.600 --> 00:05:44.240
And so I think in that season, I started praying specifics.

00:05:44.240 --> 00:05:46.520
Like I started learning how to pray for myself

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:49.760
and I would pray specifics and I would say things to God

00:05:49.760 --> 00:05:52.280
like, God, I wanna be free from people.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.760
Like I am letting these people

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:55.640
that go to the bathroom just like me,

00:05:55.640 --> 00:05:57.600
they wake up with bedhead just like me,

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:01.160
they wake up with po-chop nasty morning breath like me,

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.720
they make felt, they've fallen like me

00:06:03.720 --> 00:06:07.960
and yet here I am stuck because of what they think about me

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.160
and I wanna be free.

00:06:09.160 --> 00:06:10.720
And so I went on a journey to get free

00:06:10.720 --> 00:06:12.520
and whenever I did, man, when I tell you,

00:06:12.520 --> 00:06:15.000
I remember at 40 years old, Evan,

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:18.760
I was still at Bloomingdale's working, doing cosmetics

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.280
and the reason I got these glasses on

00:06:20.280 --> 00:06:22.560
is because my eyebrows are not on fleek.

00:06:23.760 --> 00:06:26.000
Here I am in Bloomingdale's,

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:28.440
happened to put makeup on people

00:06:28.440 --> 00:06:30.480
because I had to have a J-O-B

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:32.520
and because I walked through that divorce

00:06:32.520 --> 00:06:36.240
and man, what the enemy meant for evil,

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.000
I had to go get that job

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:42.560
and I had to go work with people and hated people

00:06:42.560 --> 00:06:45.440
and I had to learn how to do makeup on them

00:06:45.440 --> 00:06:47.280
and in that process, Evan,

00:06:47.280 --> 00:06:51.040
I started falling in love with people, their stories.

00:06:51.040 --> 00:06:53.840
I'm sitting there making $9 an hour doing makeup on people

00:06:53.840 --> 00:06:56.560
and pretending like I knew what I was doing and I didn't

00:06:56.560 --> 00:06:59.160
and for 45 minutes, I would just encourage them

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:01.600
because look, you ain't gonna have a whole head

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.880
full of makeup when I get done with you

00:07:02.880 --> 00:07:05.040
but I'm gonna need you to feel like you could own

00:07:05.040 --> 00:07:07.240
this Bloomingdale's when you walk out

00:07:07.240 --> 00:07:09.600
and so in that process of my healing,

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.560
I found out that my healing came from me loving

00:07:12.560 --> 00:07:15.240
some, loving the hell out of somebody else

00:07:15.240 --> 00:07:18.240
and so I went from hating people to loving people

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:20.160
is my favorite hobby on the planet

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.720
and I think that God has a sense of humor.

00:07:22.720 --> 00:07:25.640
He said, I'm gonna let people sleep on you

00:07:25.640 --> 00:07:27.160
because they already thought you'd have messed up

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:29.880
in the church world, can't nobody use you,

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:34.680
you are just written off, you have done the cardinal sin

00:07:34.720 --> 00:07:36.120
and they're gonna be sleeping on you

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:37.160
and while they're sleeping on you,

00:07:37.160 --> 00:07:39.480
I'm gonna be building you up for your next.

00:07:39.480 --> 00:07:40.840
I'm gonna be building you up

00:07:40.840 --> 00:07:42.560
for where I'm about to take you

00:07:42.560 --> 00:07:44.960
and you thought, Kimberly, the curtain had closed

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:46.600
but the curtain had to close

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:48.720
so I could set up for the next scene

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:51.120
and so I watched over those five years,

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:53.760
God did something and 40 years old, I remember,

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:54.920
I did a conference.

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:57.000
I don't know whatever made me do a conference.

00:07:57.000 --> 00:07:59.920
I didn't know how to preach and I was a special ed,

00:07:59.920 --> 00:08:03.960
I didn't go to Bible school and I did a conference

00:08:04.200 --> 00:08:07.320
and I named it Conquering Hell in High Heels

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:11.400
and I did that because women are the worst

00:08:11.400 --> 00:08:13.280
at walking through something

00:08:13.280 --> 00:08:15.960
and losing themselves and getting bitter Betty,

00:08:15.960 --> 00:08:17.440
really getting, letting our emotions,

00:08:17.440 --> 00:08:20.040
we can birth a whole baby out of a place

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.800
nothing should come out of

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:24.480
but yet we can't go through a breakup

00:08:24.480 --> 00:08:27.360
or go through failure or go through social media,

00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.920
scrolling on Instagram and wanting to be everybody else.

00:08:29.920 --> 00:08:31.000
I just didn't get that

